From: nura-builds
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: msm8226-samsung-s3ve3g: wcnss Wi-Fi IRQs level high

wcn36xx requests its tx and rx interrupts with IRQF_TRIGGER_HIGH, which
replaces the DT's IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING at the first probe. After a
firmware crash, remoteproc recovery probes the driver again, and mapping
the DT's edge type over the existing level mapping fails ("irq: type
mismatch, failed to map hwirq-177", "IRQ tx not found"): no Wi-Fi until
reboot. Declare them as the driver uses them.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-s3ve3g.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-s3ve3g.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-s3ve3g.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-s3ve3g.dts
@@ -421,6 +421,17 @@
 	smd-edge {
 		wcnss {
 			status = "okay";
+
+			/*
+			 * Level, as wcn36xx requests them (IRQF_TRIGGER_HIGH): with the
+			 * edge type from the DT, the second probe after a firmware
+			 * restart can't map them again ("type mismatch"), and Wi-Fi
+			 * stays gone
+			 */
+			wifi {
+				interrupts = <GIC_SPI 145 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+					     <GIC_SPI 146 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			};
 		};
 	};
 };
